 "capsule": "In 1134 the crown of Pamplona regained independence from Aragon on the death of Alfonso the Battler, restoring a Basque-Navarrese monarchy, and from the reign of Sancho VI 'the Wise' (1150-1194) the realm was formally styled the Kingdom of Navarre (Nafarroako Erresuma). Wedged between Castile, Aragon, and France, Navarre lost its Basque coastal lands to Castile in 1200 but endured under a succession of French noble houses - Champagne, Capet, Évreux, and Foix-Albret - reaching a cultural high point under Charles III 'the Noble' (1387-1425). Ferdinand II of Aragon conquered Navarre south of the Pyrenees in 1512, annexing it to Castile by 1515, while an Albret rump kingdom survived north of the Pyrenees for decades longer.",
